n sneaking in and out  of some kind of top secret volcano base  to steal some important spectrophiles  without anyone even knowing you were  there of course if it's anything like  the movies it will more likely end up  with capture  torture escape and a load of commando  lads abseiling through the ceiling  but what would an open mission structure  be without the opportunity to kit your  super spy out with all manner of  exploding stationary  or a plaster cast rocket launcher  hitman has plenty of fun gadgets to play  around with and many of them venture  into the bondy mould  exploding rubber duck anybody  so this is the perfect opportunity for  io to dig through the q  branch archives and uncover some gadgety  gems  it would also work perfectly with the  replayable multi-strand mission  structure io games are known for  imagine seeing a locked event shaft on  your first run through and coming back  equipped with a laser watch to open up  another potential opportunity for  stealth  or for a less subtle option having a go  on that profoundly dangerous looking  bagpipe flamethrower they have in the  world is not enough  [Music]  what are they even going to use that for  admittedly it's easy to think of the  over-the-top gadgets but the cold war  origins of the bond franchise do  offer up some tantalising opportunities  for more realistic espionage too  be it forging documents planting  listening devices  or taking secret photos of clandestine  meetings  but you won't find us complaining if you  get to sneak into a smurf base in a  crocodile submersible either  i don't believe we've had the pleasure  mr um reaper  tobias reaper while the similarities  between agents 47 and 97  are clear we hope io don't lean too hard  into them after all what would a bond  game be without  huge explosions car chases jet packs  little  helicopter thingies and hidden ejector  seats  a bomb game needs to make you feel like  bond and more often than not bond is  doing something bombastic  